WEBVTT

00:00:48.654 --> 00:00:49.697
Who are you?

00:00:53.534 --> 00:00:54.451
Are you

00:00:54.952 --> 00:00:55.953
Bella Jin?

00:01:08.507 --> 00:01:09.592
Bella Jin?

00:01:10.134 --> 00:01:12.386
Wait, but I thought you were in Barcelona.

00:01:13.512 --> 00:01:15.806
I got a call
that someone was looking for me.

00:01:15.890 --> 00:01:16.932
You must be the ace.

00:01:18.058 --> 00:01:19.184
Me? Yes.

00:01:19.727 --> 00:01:20.895
Anyway, I'm Bella Jin.

00:01:21.520 --> 00:01:23.522
I'm Seo Ji-woo, Director of JARIM Apparel.

00:01:24.273 --> 00:01:26.191
Let me first pay for the scarf…

00:01:26.275 --> 00:01:28.569
I'm afraid you can't.

00:01:30.571 --> 00:01:31.405
Ji-woo.
Support Admin Watch on
kissasia.cam or kisskh.org

00:01:33.073 --> 00:01:38.120
The ace here grabbed that scarf first.

00:01:39.997 --> 00:01:42.833
I did grab it first, but sure, go ahead.

00:01:42.917 --> 00:01:44.501
It's only right for us to buy it.

00:01:47.630 --> 00:01:51.133
Hey, this one. Isn't this pretty? No?

00:01:55.054 --> 00:01:56.597
You have the Delta two-piece?

00:01:57.514 --> 00:01:58.432
Yes.

00:02:00.142 --> 00:02:00.976
My mom does.

00:02:16.158 --> 00:02:16.992
Oh, hey.

00:02:17.076 --> 00:02:18.202
Okay. Here.

00:02:30.005 --> 00:02:31.090
Gracias.

00:02:33.300 --> 00:02:35.552
EPISODE 9

00:02:36.762 --> 00:02:38.931
I get the situation.

00:02:39.014 --> 00:02:42.226
Actually, when I got the call
that you wanted to see me…

00:02:42.977 --> 00:02:45.145
The call was
from Trend D's editor-in-chief.

00:02:47.022 --> 00:02:49.066
I looked up JARIM Apparel.

00:02:50.609 --> 00:02:52.736
And Daniel knows you, Ms. Seo Ji-woo.

00:02:52.820 --> 00:02:54.863
I asked him just in case. You know Daniel?

00:02:55.406 --> 00:02:58.450
Yes. My friend in England.
He runs a select shop.

00:03:01.203 --> 00:03:04.748
Daniel said I should meet you.

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:08.043
I appreciate that you came
all the way here.

00:03:08.752 --> 00:03:13.132
I think I already know what this is about.
But I have nothing to discuss with you.

00:03:13.799 --> 00:03:16.719
But since we've had coffee,
is that enough for the greeting?

00:03:17.845 --> 00:03:19.888
You're right. We've come a long way.

00:03:22.182 --> 00:03:27.730
Will you spare your time for Director Seo
to explain? We'd appreciate it.

00:03:30.941 --> 00:03:32.109
Is the scarf for your mom?

00:03:36.613 --> 00:03:38.365
You're not on good terms
with your mom, are you?

00:03:39.158 --> 00:03:40.159
Can you tell?

00:03:41.076 --> 00:03:42.327
It'll be a good gift.

00:03:42.995 --> 00:03:46.206
Málaga is nice. You might as well
check it out while you're here.

00:03:46.790 --> 00:03:48.542
It was actually nice meeting you.

00:03:48.625 --> 00:03:51.920
I'll root for JARIM Apparel. Bye now.

00:03:54.131 --> 00:03:55.591
But, Bella. I…

00:04:01.430 --> 00:04:02.931
Hey, let's follow her.

00:04:03.015 --> 00:04:03.891
Wait.

00:04:05.142 --> 00:04:06.310
We need a strategy.

00:04:17.446 --> 00:04:18.906
You said we needed a strategy.

00:04:21.784 --> 00:04:23.160
Waiting is also a strategy.

00:04:37.382 --> 00:04:41.678
Let's get up there and ring the doorbell.
We can't just wait here forever.

00:04:41.762 --> 00:04:45.057
Isn't she having dinner?
She'd come down soon.

00:04:53.816 --> 00:04:54.650
Hey!

00:05:01.240 --> 00:05:02.449
Have you been waiting here?

00:05:04.451 --> 00:05:08.163
It's a nice alley. I like watching alleys.

00:05:09.164 --> 00:05:14.545
We've been waiting for a very long time.
My legs are swollen, and I'm hungry.

00:05:21.093 --> 00:05:22.010
Do you like wine?

00:05:33.063 --> 00:05:34.439
What about you? You don't drink?

00:05:36.817 --> 00:05:41.780
I'm… taking oriental medicine.

00:05:41.864 --> 00:05:45.159
I should refrain from alcohol,
flour, or anything spicy…

00:05:47.369 --> 00:05:50.205
Ji-woo, is he your ace?

00:05:51.456 --> 00:05:52.416
Sorry?

00:05:52.875 --> 00:05:56.920
I've read your article. You two met
while doing theater together or something?

00:05:57.462 --> 00:05:58.297
Anyway,

00:06:00.507 --> 00:06:03.010
you two met when you were 20,
and it didn't end.

00:06:03.927 --> 00:06:06.221
The ace wrote about your ex-husband?

00:06:10.058 --> 00:06:13.645
I didn't publish it myself,
but technically, it was me. Yes.

00:06:14.104 --> 00:06:17.524
You two are not in love.
There's a word for it.

00:06:18.192 --> 00:06:20.360
"Baseless." Is it really baseless?

00:06:20.444 --> 00:06:22.779
Yes, that's correct. Baseless.

00:06:24.239 --> 00:06:25.365
What about now?

00:06:26.033 --> 00:06:27.910
Now we're together.

00:06:35.375 --> 00:06:38.420
Well… to continue on with my explanation…

00:06:40.422 --> 00:06:44.176
You met when you were 20,
and you're still in love?

00:06:44.259 --> 00:06:46.929
Have you ever liked any other woman?

00:06:48.013 --> 00:06:49.014
Am I too indiscreet?

00:06:49.640 --> 00:06:50.766
Well…

00:06:52.893 --> 00:06:54.770
I am kind of flustered. Yes.

00:06:55.562 --> 00:06:57.272
I need the answer.

00:07:05.781 --> 00:07:06.615
I have.

00:07:10.202 --> 00:07:12.829
The 28-year-old Seo Ji-woo.

00:07:17.584 --> 00:07:18.877
You're a selfish guy.

00:07:18.961 --> 00:07:19.795
What?

00:07:22.047 --> 00:07:22.881
He is?

00:07:22.965 --> 00:07:25.592
You grew old, from 20 to 28,

00:07:25.676 --> 00:07:28.595
all the while loving her,
and not taking your eyes off her.

00:07:28.679 --> 00:07:32.641
And even now,
you came all the way here for Seo Ji-woo,

00:07:33.642 --> 00:07:35.435
but how come you don't respect my love?

00:07:46.530 --> 00:07:47.406
Yes.

00:07:49.324 --> 00:07:54.955
I get that Pirco to you
is what Seo Ji-woo is to Lee Kyeong-do.

00:07:57.582 --> 00:07:58.583
Thanks.

00:07:59.334 --> 00:08:03.255
All right.
This is where our conversation begins.

00:08:29.239 --> 00:08:32.034
Who's going to be Lucas's successor?

00:08:32.868 --> 00:08:34.619
Judy Wong or me?

00:08:37.664 --> 00:08:38.790
Judy Wong.

00:08:40.667 --> 00:08:41.585
On what grounds?

00:08:43.503 --> 00:08:47.591
After Pirco's oldest son took over,
trouble brewed between him and Lucas.

00:08:48.508 --> 00:08:50.761
They were going in different directions.

00:08:51.636 --> 00:08:54.139
He is likely to choose Judy Wong

00:08:54.222 --> 00:08:56.475
rather than Lucas' protégé, Bella Jin.

00:08:57.351 --> 00:09:01.396
It's not that he's likely to choose her,
but it's already been decided.

00:09:04.232 --> 00:09:07.069
Why did I go to Barcelona?
I went to see it for myself.

00:09:07.819 --> 00:09:09.905
Pirco's owner was coming to Barcelona,

00:09:09.988 --> 00:09:12.824
and I heard the rumor
that Judy Wong was accompanying him.

00:09:14.159 --> 00:09:16.620
If they went there together,
hundred percent.

00:09:18.622 --> 00:09:19.664
Then you're...

00:09:20.916 --> 00:09:22.250
not coming to JARIM, are you?

00:09:23.960 --> 00:09:27.506
No, I'm not leaving Pirco.
You should put it that way.

00:09:29.466 --> 00:09:32.386
Even if I get to work under Judy Wong,
I have to accept it.

00:09:33.303 --> 00:09:35.889
It was decided in my dad's laundromat
when I was 15.

00:09:36.723 --> 00:09:40.102
I can still draw that dress from Pirco
even with my eyes closed.

00:09:41.520 --> 00:09:42.938
It is what it is.

00:09:44.147 --> 00:09:45.232
There's no other way.

00:09:55.742 --> 00:10:00.247
Let me say goodbye before I get drunk.
Thank you for coming all the way here.

00:10:02.416 --> 00:10:04.918
Thanks to you two, I'm less angry.

00:10:10.882 --> 00:10:14.469
It was a good idea
to exercise regularly, right?

00:10:14.553 --> 00:10:17.097
I mean, you jog a lot, don't you?

00:10:17.973 --> 00:10:18.807
Gosh…

00:10:20.350 --> 00:10:21.852
I'll tell everything to Mommy.

00:10:26.231 --> 00:10:27.315
Hang in there a little more.

00:10:34.406 --> 00:10:35.949
Just a little more, Kyeong-do.

00:10:36.533 --> 00:10:38.285
CAUTION
ELEVATOR OUT OF ORDER

00:10:39.286 --> 00:10:42.956
Oh, no. Are you crying? Are those tears?

00:10:43.039 --> 00:10:43.874
Is this funny?

00:10:43.957 --> 00:10:44.833
No.

00:10:44.916 --> 00:10:47.794
You can carry her too.
You can carry her up to the 2nd floor.

00:10:47.878 --> 00:10:50.046
Oh, stop talking. Hurry up.

00:10:51.715 --> 00:10:53.258
This is so narrow.

00:10:56.094 --> 00:10:57.387
Gosh, are you okay?

00:10:59.473 --> 00:11:01.349
Gosh. Shit.

00:11:02.184 --> 00:11:03.226
Damn it.

00:11:03.643 --> 00:11:08.732
Shit. Shit.

00:11:11.651 --> 00:11:12.861
Good job.

00:11:14.196 --> 00:11:15.280
We did well.

00:11:17.199 --> 00:11:21.203
We were polite.
With respect and honor, we let her go.

00:11:22.162 --> 00:11:22.996
That was cool.

00:11:26.875 --> 00:11:31.046
But we came all the way here.
You used so many of your vacation days.

00:11:32.923 --> 00:11:35.675
That was your first step as a director.
So it's a bummer.

00:11:37.928 --> 00:11:39.554
I tried to take it for granted.

00:11:40.597 --> 00:11:42.516
I'm going to take it slowly from scratch.

00:11:42.599 --> 00:11:47.187
I'll find good designers so we can be
on the Paris and New York runways.

00:11:49.689 --> 00:11:52.108
Just thinking about it
makes my stomach ticklish.

00:11:56.696 --> 00:11:59.991
Why does your stomach get ticklish
when you have happy thoughts?

00:12:01.076 --> 00:12:03.453
-You remember that?
-Hey, what was that for?

00:12:04.412 --> 00:12:07.958
You still have strength left?
You definitely could have carried her.

00:12:08.041 --> 00:12:10.210
Seo Ji-woo, don't move.

00:12:10.293 --> 00:12:12.254
Don't be like this. I'm hungry.

00:12:12.337 --> 00:12:13.380
-Engage your spine.
-No…

00:12:13.463 --> 00:12:14.673
-Be ready.
-But…

00:12:14.756 --> 00:12:16.049
-All right.
-No, I…

00:12:19.052 --> 00:12:20.804
Walk to the runway like this. Okay?

00:12:20.887 --> 00:12:23.557
Hey, come down. You'll break my backbone.

00:12:44.327 --> 00:12:45.662
CEO Seo.

00:12:45.745 --> 00:12:50.041
She's keeping it a secret and fighting it.
But the truth is, she's getting worse.

00:12:52.252 --> 00:12:57.340
How could I not know when I'm watching her
so closely? It's kind of pitiful.

00:12:59.259 --> 00:13:02.178
Don't mind Seo Ji-woo's word
on getting rid of MANZAAR.

00:13:03.513 --> 00:13:07.851
You've seen it too.
Getting rid of MANZAAR,

00:13:07.934 --> 00:13:11.062
that's her first mission? My goodness.

00:13:11.146 --> 00:13:12.731
Isn't that brilliant and bold?

00:13:15.275 --> 00:13:16.484
Executive Director Choi.

00:13:17.068 --> 00:13:21.573
When Seo Ji-woo returns from Spain,
she'll soon look ridiculous.

00:13:21.656 --> 00:13:24.534
How is she going to scout
a luxury brand designer?

00:13:24.618 --> 00:13:26.911
She probably went because she had a plan.

00:13:26.995 --> 00:13:28.163
Do you trust her?

00:13:28.246 --> 00:13:29.122
Not yet.

00:13:29.205 --> 00:13:30.040
That's what I mean.

00:13:30.123 --> 00:13:32.584
Still, I'm looking forward to it.

00:13:33.710 --> 00:13:37.714
She might not sell the company
for a dirt cheap price.

00:13:38.340 --> 00:13:42.802
I'm getting the thought
that Seo Ji-woo could be the dark horse.

00:13:44.304 --> 00:13:45.221
Executive Director Choi.

00:13:45.305 --> 00:13:46.222
Can't you feel it?

00:13:47.223 --> 00:13:49.142
The atmosphere is brightening up.

00:13:49.225 --> 00:13:51.186
Young employees are supporting Seo Ji-woo.

00:13:52.145 --> 00:13:53.355
Director Seo Ji-woo said

00:13:53.438 --> 00:13:56.900
she'd bring a luxury brand designer
who lives up to their name.

00:13:57.942 --> 00:14:01.112
You think she brightened up the mood
without any plans?

00:14:02.322 --> 00:14:03.490
Seriously?

00:14:04.908 --> 00:14:08.912
Right now, I'm even thinking

00:14:09.663 --> 00:14:12.290
that JARIM's second prime is coming.

00:14:13.500 --> 00:14:14.501
What if she fails

00:14:15.543 --> 00:14:16.461
to bring a designer?

00:14:17.796 --> 00:14:19.339
Then Seo Ji-woo

00:14:19.923 --> 00:14:23.093
will turn out to be digging her own grave.

00:14:36.064 --> 00:14:36.898
Here.

00:14:41.069 --> 00:14:42.570
Do you want milk?

00:14:50.412 --> 00:14:51.329
Kyeong-do.

00:14:54.165 --> 00:14:55.166
Yes?

00:14:56.126 --> 00:14:59.254
Move your damn head.
You're blocking the tiny sea view we have.

00:15:03.174 --> 00:15:05.427
-Happy now?
-Yes. Nice.

00:15:05.510 --> 00:15:06.511
Yes. Good job.

00:15:11.307 --> 00:15:14.310
I wonder if Bella Jin is okay.
We should say goodbye before we go.

00:15:14.394 --> 00:15:15.520
Should I call her?

00:15:18.982 --> 00:15:21.443
JOIN ME TO RELIEVE YOUR HANGOVER?

00:15:22.360 --> 00:15:24.446
She wants to relieve a hangover together.

00:15:42.589 --> 00:15:43.423
Lucas's number.

00:15:45.091 --> 00:15:46.801
I was wasted last night.

00:15:46.885 --> 00:15:51.931
I was struck by the Delta two-piece
and by the Seo Ji-woo and Pirco metaphor.

00:15:52.015 --> 00:15:55.059
I got so excited that I talked to Lucas
on the phone for an hour.

00:15:58.438 --> 00:15:59.856
He hasn't decided where to go.

00:16:01.065 --> 00:16:03.067
I recommended you
under the influence of wine.

00:16:07.071 --> 00:16:09.073
Thank you for carrying me
to the 5th floor.

00:16:11.701 --> 00:16:13.036
He said it's interesting

00:16:13.119 --> 00:16:15.663
that you spotted the Delta scarf
at a street stall in Málaga.

00:16:16.873 --> 00:16:18.124
By interesting, he means…

00:16:18.208 --> 00:16:22.170
When Lucas likes a result,
he calls it interesting.

00:16:22.754 --> 00:16:23.922
Call him.

00:16:24.005 --> 00:16:26.049
He wouldn't give you an immediate answer,

00:16:27.509 --> 00:16:28.718
but give him time.

00:16:30.136 --> 00:16:31.805
Interesting…

00:16:44.859 --> 00:16:49.239
You know, every country
has different alleys. I like it here too.

00:16:50.240 --> 00:16:51.908
What's your favorite?

00:16:53.701 --> 00:16:55.620
The alley next to Somang Laundromat?

00:16:57.997 --> 00:16:59.707
Oh, right. Let's buy snacks.

00:16:59.791 --> 00:17:00.875
Why? Are you hungry?

00:17:01.918 --> 00:17:03.127
No, not that.

00:17:04.379 --> 00:17:06.756
Something you'd find
in the department store.

00:17:06.840 --> 00:17:08.049
Pretty and delicious.

00:17:09.509 --> 00:17:10.885
Department store…

00:17:11.386 --> 00:17:13.096
Pretty and delicious?

00:17:13.179 --> 00:17:16.391
Not from a real one,
but if we could find something like that.

00:17:18.685 --> 00:17:21.813
Then… a dessert?

00:17:25.441 --> 00:17:27.277
LETTER OF INTENT TO SUE

00:17:27.360 --> 00:17:33.575
JARIM DIRECTOR KANG MIN-WOO

00:17:34.951 --> 00:17:36.244
Hey, CEO Bae.

00:17:36.995 --> 00:17:40.373
You scared me. Is this really necessary?

00:17:40.456 --> 00:17:43.501
If this doesn't get resolved,
I'm going to talk to CEO Seo Ji-yeon.

00:17:43.585 --> 00:17:44.836
No!

00:17:47.213 --> 00:17:50.425
We're almost there.
If you do this, we'll both--

00:17:50.508 --> 00:17:52.051
I heard Seo Ji-woo went to Spain.

00:17:52.135 --> 00:17:56.055
She's working hard.
If it's like this, I can't vouch for you.

00:17:57.015 --> 00:17:58.600
Sorry. I'm still in a meeting.

00:18:12.906 --> 00:18:14.782
ACCUSED
KANG MIN-WOO

00:18:43.770 --> 00:18:45.229
What are you going to do about this?

00:18:47.440 --> 00:18:48.858
Hello.

00:18:48.942 --> 00:18:51.361
Oh, hello. One second, okay?

00:18:51.444 --> 00:18:52.904
-Hey, look.
-Yes.

00:18:52.987 --> 00:18:56.824
I asked to remove the stain, not smear it.
How am I supposed to wear this?

00:18:58.368 --> 00:19:01.829
That's why I explained it to you
in the first place.

00:19:02.497 --> 00:19:05.541
It's not easy to remove the red oil stain.

00:19:05.625 --> 00:19:08.586
I also explained to you
that a dark fabric could be bleached.

00:19:08.670 --> 00:19:11.464
"Could" means there was a way
to prevent it, no?

00:19:12.382 --> 00:19:15.802
Because you kept the stain for too long,
it wasn't easy to remove.

00:19:15.885 --> 00:19:18.429
Then you should've said
you couldn't do it.

00:19:18.513 --> 00:19:20.390
This is my favorite dress.

00:19:20.473 --> 00:19:21.724
Damn it.

00:19:21.808 --> 00:19:24.018
You must've really liked it.

00:19:24.560 --> 00:19:26.104
Who are you to barge in?

00:19:26.729 --> 00:19:27.647
Sorry.

00:19:29.524 --> 00:19:31.818
What do you want me to do?

00:19:31.901 --> 00:19:33.569
Why are you asking me?

00:19:33.653 --> 00:19:37.407
That's what I need to know.
Are you going to get me the same dress?

00:19:37.490 --> 00:19:39.951
You won't be able to find the same one.

00:19:40.034 --> 00:19:42.620
That's too old,
so you can't even find it in the outlets.

00:19:42.704 --> 00:19:44.580
Hey, who are you to keep barging in?

00:19:44.664 --> 00:19:48.209
Well, it's just an unfortunate situation…

00:19:48.292 --> 00:19:51.504
Then mind your own business and walk away.

00:19:51.587 --> 00:19:54.007
Wait, this is from JARIM Apparel.
Isn't it?

00:19:54.090 --> 00:19:56.175
You got nothing else to do?
You think this is funny?

00:19:56.259 --> 00:19:57.760
I do have other things to do.

00:19:58.302 --> 00:20:02.849
And so do they. It seems you're the one
with nothing else to do.

00:20:04.142 --> 00:20:06.978
I'll call the police.
Are you out of your mind?

00:20:07.061 --> 00:20:10.189
Take this and get whatever dress you want
from our store.

00:20:12.859 --> 00:20:14.235
JARIM
SEO JI-WOO

00:20:14.986 --> 00:20:17.321
Which store is the closest?
I'll let them know.

00:20:17.947 --> 00:20:21.284
The closest store… I'll have to look.

00:20:22.368 --> 00:20:24.162
Can I really take whatever I want?

00:20:24.245 --> 00:20:25.496
Yes.

00:20:26.956 --> 00:20:29.000
Even the Lusae store in Cheongdam-dong?

00:20:29.751 --> 00:20:31.002
Yes, I'll call them.

00:20:33.254 --> 00:20:35.006
Wait, you need to pay before you go.

00:20:35.089 --> 00:20:36.132
What?

00:20:36.215 --> 00:20:38.217
For removing the stain and dry cleaning.

00:20:40.261 --> 00:20:41.095
Wait.

00:20:41.679 --> 00:20:46.142
Don't forget to take this.
Your favorite dress.

00:20:56.277 --> 00:20:57.320
Well…

00:20:58.738 --> 00:21:01.991
Here. I didn't buy it
in a department store basement floor,

00:21:02.075 --> 00:21:03.951
but from a good place near my work.

00:21:08.331 --> 00:21:09.791
The lady Kyeong-do's seeing.

00:21:12.376 --> 00:21:13.377
Hello.

00:21:14.212 --> 00:21:15.213
It's too cramped in here--

00:21:15.296 --> 00:21:17.590
No. I was going to leave
after giving you this.

00:21:18.341 --> 00:21:19.175
Are you busy?

00:21:19.967 --> 00:21:20.802
No.

00:21:31.938 --> 00:21:35.233
I wanted to get something from Málaga,
but I didn't find anything good.

00:21:36.484 --> 00:21:38.069
Is that in Spain?

00:21:38.152 --> 00:21:39.070
Yes.

00:21:40.404 --> 00:21:42.031
Kyeong-do was very helpful.

00:21:42.115 --> 00:21:43.449
Did things go well?

00:21:44.909 --> 00:21:49.288
That is… kind of iffy.
I haven't received the answer yet.

00:21:49.372 --> 00:21:50.790
Did Kyeong-do go to Spain?

00:21:50.873 --> 00:21:52.834
I told you the other day.

00:21:55.837 --> 00:21:58.089
-You must be anxious.
-I can't even sleep.

00:21:58.172 --> 00:21:59.882
It must be very important.

00:22:00.591 --> 00:22:04.470
Yes. This is my first project
since I joined the company.

00:22:04.554 --> 00:22:06.013
I'm worried about it.

00:22:06.764 --> 00:22:10.184
Gosh, even running a laundromat this size
is not easy.

00:22:10.268 --> 00:22:12.854
A company that big must be even harder.

00:22:12.937 --> 00:22:13.771
Oh, no...

00:22:15.565 --> 00:22:17.483
I'm sorry. Excuse me…

00:22:19.735 --> 00:22:20.653
Who keeps calling…

00:22:24.407 --> 00:22:28.786
Lucas. Mother. Wait. Excuse me. Sorry.

00:22:31.205 --> 00:22:32.165
Lucas?

00:22:33.541 --> 00:22:35.042
Do you think he fell for that?

00:22:42.550 --> 00:22:43.384
Did she leave?

00:22:44.468 --> 00:22:46.137
But her bag is here.

00:22:55.855 --> 00:22:58.232
Please excuse me…

00:22:58.941 --> 00:22:59.775
Oh, my!

00:23:04.488 --> 00:23:06.240
Excuse me, Father.

00:23:06.324 --> 00:23:08.284
Yes… Yes, sure.

00:23:10.995 --> 00:23:14.165
Lucas is coming. He's coming to JARIM!

00:23:14.248 --> 00:23:16.000
-Lucas?
-It's a good thing, right?

00:23:16.083 --> 00:23:18.169
This is totally awesome.

00:23:18.252 --> 00:23:22.256
Being together with you two
brings me good luck. This is amazing!

00:23:24.467 --> 00:23:27.845
Oh, my God. Let me call Kyeong-do.

00:23:32.850 --> 00:23:36.854
Hey, Kyeong-do. This is crazy.
Don't be surprised.

00:23:38.105 --> 00:23:39.565
Lucas is coming!

00:23:41.567 --> 00:23:43.361
-Ouch…
-Oh, no.

00:23:43.444 --> 00:23:45.154
I was so surprised.

00:23:48.324 --> 00:23:50.910
I was more surprised
that you went to the laundromat.

00:23:50.993 --> 00:23:53.996
That place has good energy.
I think that place is a lucky location.

00:23:54.956 --> 00:23:56.207
Did you let the CEO know?

00:23:56.290 --> 00:23:58.334
My sister is excited.

00:23:58.417 --> 00:24:01.128
She's busy setting her schedule
to meet Lucas.

00:24:02.672 --> 00:24:06.425
Our laundromat
is indeed a lucky location, but--

00:24:06.509 --> 00:24:09.512
Things are turning out well
because I met you, Kyeong-do.

00:24:09.595 --> 00:24:11.931
That's right. Here.

00:24:20.231 --> 00:24:23.234
Speaking of which,
I need a painting of you as well.

00:24:24.277 --> 00:24:26.445
No, just take that with you.

00:24:26.529 --> 00:24:28.572
No, that should be here.

00:24:28.656 --> 00:24:31.951
Since you have good energy,
I should have your portrait in my house.

00:24:32.576 --> 00:24:35.413
Maybe about the size of…

00:24:37.290 --> 00:24:38.207
a photograph?

00:24:39.250 --> 00:24:41.919
-Why is mine small?
-It doesn't match my house design.

00:24:42.795 --> 00:24:44.505
A small one next to my bed would be great.

00:24:44.588 --> 00:24:46.757
Hey, my house also has a design.

00:24:46.841 --> 00:24:49.593
You're on a lease.
But I live in my own house.

00:24:50.761 --> 00:24:51.637
That's not logical.

00:24:51.721 --> 00:24:54.265
Why are you nitpicking?
It is if I say it is.

00:24:56.017 --> 00:24:57.184
Just finish your drink.

00:25:03.274 --> 00:25:04.942
Is this what people call
an after-work drink?

00:25:05.026 --> 00:25:06.986
-You kind of get fake drunk, right?
-No.

00:25:09.488 --> 00:25:10.323
Imagine you do.

00:25:10.406 --> 00:25:12.074
-Yes, I do.
-Right?

00:25:12.158 --> 00:25:13.200
-Yes.
-Okay.

00:25:13.284 --> 00:25:14.368
Gosh…

00:25:19.790 --> 00:25:20.833
One more!

00:25:51.697 --> 00:25:54.492
Sorry for calling you out so early.

00:25:54.992 --> 00:25:57.870
Better than getting stopped out of nowhere
in front of my house.

00:25:58.621 --> 00:26:00.831
It's nice and quiet.

00:26:07.546 --> 00:26:08.547
Mr. Bae Jun-soo?

00:26:15.554 --> 00:26:18.933
Min-woo got worked up and called me
when he got the notice.

00:26:20.768 --> 00:26:24.605
You probably won't get
that 30 billion won back.

00:26:26.440 --> 00:26:28.734
Director Seo Ji-woo is doing pretty well.

00:26:28.818 --> 00:26:33.155
She scouted the lead designer of Pirco,
the company is hyped up.

00:26:34.782 --> 00:26:37.118
We won't be selling the company.

00:26:39.161 --> 00:26:41.205
Thanks to you, I could secure my credit.

00:26:42.164 --> 00:26:44.291
If I had counted on Min-woo
and kept going…

00:26:46.335 --> 00:26:48.045
I asked you to see me today

00:26:49.088 --> 00:26:53.759
because I wanted to ask you
if you could invest the budget in us.

00:26:55.386 --> 00:26:57.430
I'm going to meet Designer Lucas.

00:26:58.013 --> 00:27:01.934
The key deal points are already agreed on.
I'll meet him to sign the contract.

00:27:02.601 --> 00:27:06.230
Once Lucas arrives,
JARIM will change completely.

00:27:06.313 --> 00:27:08.357
I'm sure you know it better than I do.

00:27:16.907 --> 00:27:21.203
NAMU ART ACADEMY

00:27:21.287 --> 00:27:23.080
Jeong-min, you're awesome.

00:27:23.664 --> 00:27:26.167
Go wild, okay?
It's not a good look to babysit it.

00:27:26.250 --> 00:27:29.336
As if this is nothing,
just ride it nonchalantly, okay?

00:27:29.420 --> 00:27:32.006
You should've got a used one.
What if I scratch it?

00:27:32.089 --> 00:27:34.717
I wouldn't let Actor Cha ride a used one.

00:27:35.259 --> 00:27:37.970
Hey, if I get the delivery guy role,
I'd be the best.

00:27:38.721 --> 00:27:41.682
You dream so small.

00:27:41.765 --> 00:27:43.684
Ride with a pretty girl, not food--

00:27:43.767 --> 00:27:46.228
-I can't ride with him every day.
-Honey.

00:27:46.312 --> 00:27:49.648
Whatever. Forget it. I'm getting dizzy.
Try it. Ride it.

00:27:51.192 --> 00:27:53.486
Wait. It's Hyeon-u. It's my boss.

00:27:54.195 --> 00:27:55.821
CEO Im. Hello. How are you?

00:27:58.491 --> 00:28:00.284
What? Really? Is he hurt badly?

00:28:01.952 --> 00:28:03.954
That's a relief. Yes.

00:28:06.332 --> 00:28:08.459
Yeah. I understudied it for quite long.

00:28:10.294 --> 00:28:12.546
I can still recite it
at the drop of a hat.

00:28:13.756 --> 00:28:15.341
Yes. Okay. Yup.

00:28:15.966 --> 00:28:19.011
Yes. Goodbye. Yes, sir. Bye.

00:28:26.560 --> 00:28:28.395
Why? Is someone hurt?

00:28:29.355 --> 00:28:30.523
Waiting for Godot.

00:28:31.273 --> 00:28:33.734
It's near the end of the run,
but the lead role is hurt.

00:28:34.485 --> 00:28:36.111
Oh, no. Is it serious?

00:28:36.195 --> 00:28:37.655
No, not that serious.

00:28:39.156 --> 00:28:40.157
But you know,

00:28:41.116 --> 00:28:42.952
I understudied the play twice.

00:28:43.035 --> 00:28:44.954
-Yes.
-What's understudying?

00:28:45.037 --> 00:28:47.873
You know, the replacement
when the actor can't make it.

00:28:47.957 --> 00:28:51.210
Since you never know what might happen,
you memorize everything.

00:28:51.752 --> 00:28:52.836
-Right, Woo-sik?
-Yes.

00:28:53.671 --> 00:28:54.713
So…

00:28:56.549 --> 00:28:59.802
He's telling me to take over
for the rest of the show.

00:29:09.770 --> 00:29:11.689
Hey, you!

00:29:11.772 --> 00:29:13.941
He told me to come now.
I'm in a hurry. Manager.

00:29:14.024 --> 00:29:17.486
Okay. Where to? Where is it?
But I don't have a motorcycle license.

00:29:17.570 --> 00:29:18.445
You idiot. Get off.

00:29:18.529 --> 00:29:19.613
I do. I have a license.

00:29:19.697 --> 00:29:22.866
Honey. You need to calm down.
Relax. Calm down!

00:29:22.950 --> 00:29:27.162
Get ready for the class. I…
Let me go get ready for the play.

00:29:27.246 --> 00:29:29.540
-For the play.
-Woo-sik, you're so hot.

00:29:29.623 --> 00:29:31.458
-Go. Go now.
-Okay, I'll go now.

00:29:31.542 --> 00:29:35.713
-Be careful. You've got this. Drive safe!
-Yes. Bye. I did it!

00:29:40.301 --> 00:29:42.261
Is he riding that to work?

00:29:42.803 --> 00:29:44.597
Does he even know how to get there?

00:29:50.352 --> 00:29:52.771
Chinese food for lunch is too heavy. Jeez.

00:29:55.024 --> 00:29:58.527
What did the food do wrong?
Perhaps it's your heart that's heavy?

00:29:58.611 --> 00:30:01.989
I have no appetite.
I don't want to exercise either. Shit.

00:30:08.454 --> 00:30:11.498
Well… Min-woo. You know, about last time,

00:30:11.582 --> 00:30:15.252
what I said when I was drunk.
You know you must keep it a secret, right?

00:30:17.004 --> 00:30:18.255
Hey, is that true though?

00:30:19.173 --> 00:30:22.217
I can't tell if you got too drunk
and talked nonsense.

00:30:22.718 --> 00:30:23.552
That makes no sense.

00:30:23.636 --> 00:30:26.472
My father was Chairman Seo's best friend.

00:30:27.097 --> 00:30:30.517
The old folks who run companies
tend to take each other's side.

00:30:30.601 --> 00:30:32.227
Only my father knows about this.

00:30:33.062 --> 00:30:36.440
One time, Chairman Seo got drunk
and cried his eyes out because of it.

00:30:37.941 --> 00:30:41.028
But it's strange. Why did your family
accept someone like that?

00:30:41.111 --> 00:30:43.947
Maybe because I have a lot of flaws,
damn it.

00:30:44.615 --> 00:30:48.160
I used to do drugs and beat people.
I caused a lot of trouble.

00:30:48.994 --> 00:30:50.704
Still, why would your father do that?

00:30:50.788 --> 00:30:55.376
But Chairman Seo did adore her
like she was his own. I know that.

00:30:56.502 --> 00:30:59.004
Min-woo, promise me
you must not tell anyone, okay?

00:30:59.963 --> 00:31:00.881
Ji-yeon probably knows.

00:31:01.340 --> 00:31:04.426
When I hint you the timing,
talk to her for me, will you?

00:31:05.552 --> 00:31:09.682
I'm not interested in JARIM at all, okay?

00:31:09.765 --> 00:31:12.142
It seems
Seo Ji-woo scored something in Spain.

00:31:12.226 --> 00:31:15.145
Once this gets out,
how could she run the company?

00:31:15.229 --> 00:31:16.313
She's not a real daughter.

00:31:20.150 --> 00:31:22.152
So what are you going to do about it?

00:31:22.903 --> 00:31:25.114
It's over. You might as well move on.

00:31:25.197 --> 00:31:27.491
I need her back, you know?

00:31:27.574 --> 00:31:31.954
If she grows old with that lowlife,
her life will become a real mess.

00:31:33.163 --> 00:31:34.123
I'll get her back.

00:31:41.422 --> 00:31:42.715
This mapo tofu is good.

00:32:00.482 --> 00:32:05.237
GENETIC TESTS FOR TWO SISTERS
WHO SHARE THE SAME MOTHER

00:32:08.407 --> 00:32:10.909
How am I supposed to test the DNA
with a dead man?

00:32:12.202 --> 00:32:13.704
I can't open the coffin.

00:32:15.956 --> 00:32:17.791
Damn it.

00:32:37.394 --> 00:32:40.230
What's the point of having my portrait?
This is the best.

00:32:42.733 --> 00:32:44.276
This…

00:32:46.361 --> 00:32:51.575
Still, give it a try. You might find it.

00:32:51.658 --> 00:32:52.493
Okay.

00:32:53.160 --> 00:32:55.954
There's nothing… What's in here… Wait.

00:33:24.942 --> 00:33:27.861
Whenever my sister was seeing someone,
she used to make paper cranes.

00:33:27.945 --> 00:33:30.864
Every time she got a new boyfriend,
she made a thousand of them.

00:33:32.616 --> 00:33:35.619
Would she still make them? She's 60 now.

00:33:38.539 --> 00:33:42.000
Hey, are you going to put them in a jar
and give it to someone?

00:33:43.335 --> 00:33:44.878
Do women still like it these days?

00:33:44.962 --> 00:33:47.923
I've only given a jar
filled with rolled bills.

00:33:48.549 --> 00:33:51.009
Origami is so old.

00:33:51.093 --> 00:33:54.263
Mind your own businesses.
Why are you wasting paper?

00:33:54.346 --> 00:33:57.766
You know, I've been only writing articles
about economy.

00:33:57.850 --> 00:34:00.519
And now that I see something
so uneconomical and unproductive,

00:34:00.602 --> 00:34:03.188
I'm getting a dopamine rush.
Didn't I do a good job?

00:34:03.981 --> 00:34:05.691
That's pretty good.

00:34:05.774 --> 00:34:06.984
Your sister taught you?

00:34:07.067 --> 00:34:08.193
The flowers.

00:34:08.277 --> 00:34:09.778
You were making these?

00:34:10.445 --> 00:34:12.197
Be romantic and make the flowers.

00:34:13.031 --> 00:34:14.408
Are you on an expedition to my team?

00:34:15.617 --> 00:34:18.704
I wonder if our manager is back.

00:34:18.787 --> 00:34:19.663
The chair…

00:34:21.248 --> 00:34:22.082
What are you doing?

00:34:22.165 --> 00:34:25.085
I've started a new hobby
using the lunch hour.

00:34:30.132 --> 00:34:30.966
And you?

00:34:32.259 --> 00:34:33.886
I'm trying it out
because it's interesting.

00:34:35.512 --> 00:34:36.346
Okay.

00:34:36.847 --> 00:34:38.891
I don't even have the energy
to make a fuss.

00:34:38.974 --> 00:34:41.768
You're groundbreaking in so many ways,
Lee Kyeong-do.

00:34:43.270 --> 00:34:45.063
The lunch hour is up.

00:34:45.147 --> 00:34:46.565
-Let's get back to work.
-Yes.

00:34:49.484 --> 00:34:51.236
Just out of curiosity,

00:34:51.320 --> 00:34:53.864
-Are you going to put them in a nice jar?
-Yes.

00:34:53.947 --> 00:34:56.241
Not just these little pieces of paper,
are you?

00:34:56.325 --> 00:34:58.827
They're origami roses,
not pieces of paper.

00:34:59.411 --> 00:35:02.873
Making them one by one
with heart and sincerity.

00:35:02.956 --> 00:35:06.001
Hey, she can't even throw it out later.
It's useless.

00:35:06.084 --> 00:35:08.211
Are you going to add something shiny too?

00:35:09.212 --> 00:35:11.757
-Like what?
-What do you think, Doo-jin?

00:35:11.840 --> 00:35:13.967
-A rose gold necklace?
-Bingo.

00:35:14.051 --> 00:35:16.094
A diamond ring of a modest size?

00:35:16.178 --> 00:35:17.179
Good.

00:35:17.262 --> 00:35:20.474
Luxury brand earrings, bracelets,
et cetera.

00:35:20.557 --> 00:35:22.142
-Thank you.
-Shallow.

00:35:22.225 --> 00:35:23.727
-What…
-Excuse me?

00:35:26.647 --> 00:35:30.484
I'd welcome these origami roses
made with such care for me.

00:35:30.567 --> 00:35:34.529
Is that so? Then make them with him
in the meeting room every day at lunch.

00:35:34.613 --> 00:35:37.741
I don't like to make them myself.
Here, Assistant Manager.

00:35:37.824 --> 00:35:38.700
Yes.

00:35:39.576 --> 00:35:41.078
Thank you.

00:35:41.662 --> 00:35:43.914
Hey, lunch time's up,
let's get back to work.

00:35:46.041 --> 00:35:47.376
Work now.

00:35:47.459 --> 00:35:49.378
Hobbies are for lunchtime.

00:35:58.387 --> 00:36:00.806
Not just these little pieces of paper,
are you?

00:36:00.889 --> 00:36:03.100
Jeez. Damn it.

00:36:28.917 --> 00:36:31.086
Is this a lucky draw or what?

00:36:35.048 --> 00:36:38.552
Making them one by one
with heart and sincerity.

00:36:38.635 --> 00:36:41.596
Hey, she can't even throw it out later.
It's useless.

00:36:43.140 --> 00:36:45.517
Are you going to add something shiny too?

00:36:52.024 --> 00:36:55.110
Forget it. Gosh. Jeez.

00:36:56.653 --> 00:36:57.487
Jeez.

00:36:58.405 --> 00:37:00.657
WAITING FOR GODOT
CHA WOO-SIK

00:37:00.741 --> 00:37:02.367
Dong-won. Go stand there.

00:37:06.455 --> 00:37:09.708
Hey, Woo-sik gets to perform
by chance, right?

00:37:11.043 --> 00:37:14.880
What do you mean "by chance"? A prepared
actor is getting his moment to shine.

00:37:15.589 --> 00:37:16.757
The original actor got hurt--

00:37:16.840 --> 00:37:18.383
You need to talk less.

00:37:19.051 --> 00:37:20.343
Dong-won, isn't your dad cool?

00:37:20.427 --> 00:37:21.553
Yes, he's cool.

00:37:22.554 --> 00:37:24.639
-All right. Let's go.
-He's handsome.

00:37:25.557 --> 00:37:27.893
Didn't you play the Boy in this play?

00:37:27.976 --> 00:37:29.227
You didn't even come to watch.

00:37:29.853 --> 00:37:32.522
"Godot is not coming.
Ji-woo is not coming."

00:37:38.653 --> 00:37:42.115
How many times did you watch this play?
Only when you wrote that article?

00:37:45.786 --> 00:37:49.164
Sometimes at the national theater
whenever it came to my mind.

00:37:52.042 --> 00:37:54.127
This stop is the national theater.

00:37:55.337 --> 00:37:57.255
WAITING FOR GODOT

00:37:57.339 --> 00:37:59.716
The next stop
is Songjeong Integrated Center.

00:38:04.179 --> 00:38:05.388
NATIONAL THEATER

00:38:10.102 --> 00:38:12.687
WAITING FOR GODOT

00:38:21.571 --> 00:38:22.405
Sorry.

00:38:26.910 --> 00:38:30.288
WAITING FOR GODOT
HAEUM THEATER

00:38:36.628 --> 00:38:37.796
Hurry up.

00:38:44.010 --> 00:38:46.388
WAITING FOR GODOT
HAEUM NATIONAL THEATER

00:38:52.686 --> 00:38:54.020
WAITING FOR GODOT

00:39:04.656 --> 00:39:06.616
JANGCHUNG SNACK BAR

00:39:15.125 --> 00:39:17.627
JANGCHUNG SNACK BAR

00:39:23.508 --> 00:39:25.385
WAITING FOR GODOT

00:39:37.898 --> 00:39:40.692
WAITING FOR GODOT
FINAL PERFORMANCE

00:39:40.775 --> 00:39:42.319
Waiting for Godot?

00:39:42.402 --> 00:39:46.990
Yes, it's been performed every year,
but this year will be the last one.

00:39:48.408 --> 00:39:50.118
Why should we write about this?

00:39:51.161 --> 00:39:55.415
They were in deficit due to low turnout,
yet the play ran for ten years.

00:39:56.166 --> 00:40:00.795
But now, they can't keep going anymore,
so it'll be their last show.

00:40:02.297 --> 00:40:06.551
It's meaningful. A theater that put on
a good play despite no profit.

00:40:06.635 --> 00:40:08.386
I thought it'd be a good article.

00:40:08.929 --> 00:40:10.096
Kyeong-do will write

00:40:11.514 --> 00:40:13.850
about Godot?

00:40:17.395 --> 00:40:18.730
What does that smile mean?

00:40:21.524 --> 00:40:25.237
I remembered someone else
also saying Godot sounded like Kyeong-do.

00:40:26.738 --> 00:40:29.074
-It's personal, isn't it?
-No.

00:40:32.202 --> 00:40:33.161
It is.

00:40:36.873 --> 00:40:37.749
Sure, go with it.

00:40:38.750 --> 00:40:40.210
It better be good.

00:40:40.293 --> 00:40:42.212
Yup. I'll do my best.

00:40:43.838 --> 00:40:44.756
Thank you.

00:40:44.839 --> 00:40:48.468
You've been showing it
despite the long deficit.

00:40:48.551 --> 00:40:51.137
What kept you going?

00:40:51.221 --> 00:40:54.683
It's not that I endured it
because I had any specific reason.

00:40:55.225 --> 00:40:57.519
"Just for this year. Just one more year."

00:40:58.019 --> 00:40:59.646
Then it's been ten years.

00:41:01.856 --> 00:41:05.402
It seems the cast didn't change much
over the decade. Am I right?

00:41:05.485 --> 00:41:07.070
That's part of it.

00:41:07.153 --> 00:41:09.698
After the show ends,
we get some soju and go home.

00:41:09.781 --> 00:41:12.617
Then the next year, we gather again.

00:41:12.701 --> 00:41:14.786
Preparing Godot was…

00:41:15.662 --> 00:41:17.038
How can I put it?

00:41:19.249 --> 00:41:21.209
It's not something you do out of duty,

00:41:21.293 --> 00:41:24.546
but something you're doing
before you even realize. Is that it?

00:41:28.591 --> 00:41:31.761
When the article is out, buy the paper.

00:41:31.845 --> 00:41:34.014
And keep it. It's our history.

00:41:34.097 --> 00:41:35.140
Godot.

00:41:36.975 --> 00:41:38.727
I see. Then are you ending it too?

00:41:39.686 --> 00:41:40.645
Ending what?

00:41:40.729 --> 00:41:43.690
Waiting For Godot is closing.
Are you moving on as well?

00:41:46.901 --> 00:41:50.238
Honey. That sounds like
he couldn't go on a date because of her.

00:41:50.322 --> 00:41:51.239
Read the room.

00:41:52.032 --> 00:41:54.617
Why bother? That's not like you.

00:41:56.202 --> 00:41:59.748
Right. Move on, will you?
She disappeared without a trace.

00:41:59.831 --> 00:42:02.000
If you know where she is,
you'd at least visit her.

00:42:02.083 --> 00:42:05.128
For goodness' sake,
move on already, will you?

00:42:05.211 --> 00:42:06.171
I already have.

00:42:08.340 --> 00:42:10.008
Okay, let's call it that.

00:42:10.091 --> 00:42:11.760
-Here.
-No, I mean it.

00:42:13.094 --> 00:42:15.889
Now, Waiting for Godot is over.

00:42:16.598 --> 00:42:17.807
Everything is over.

00:42:18.475 --> 00:42:20.060
Everyone, raise your glasses. Cheers.

00:42:20.727 --> 00:42:22.187
-Cheers.
-Sure, cheers.

00:42:22.812 --> 00:42:23.646
Cheers.

00:42:30.236 --> 00:42:34.074
We've come a long way.
Is it finally over tomorrow?

00:42:35.075 --> 00:42:37.702
You must be getting tired.

00:42:38.244 --> 00:42:40.205
It's not that I'm tired.

00:42:41.122 --> 00:42:43.458
I've simply been walking forward.

00:42:45.210 --> 00:42:49.506
I don't know what I passed
or what passed me.

00:42:50.673 --> 00:42:51.883
Everything

00:42:53.134 --> 00:42:54.844
sounds like an old song.

00:42:57.013 --> 00:43:02.185
The lyrics are gone, but the melody keeps
ringing in my mouth. A song like that.

00:43:03.561 --> 00:43:08.274
I don't even know if I sang it
or if someone else sang it.

00:43:09.359 --> 00:43:10.735
I don't know anymore.

00:43:24.541 --> 00:43:26.459
WAITING FOR GODOT
HAEUM NATIONAL THEATER

00:43:44.436 --> 00:43:46.187
-Mr. Kim.
-Yes?

00:44:16.509 --> 00:44:18.052
Do you like this play that much?

00:44:19.137 --> 00:44:21.973
You watch it every time you come to Korea.
Is it still fun?

00:44:23.349 --> 00:44:24.434
It's boring.

00:44:26.686 --> 00:44:28.646
Hurry up. We're late.

00:44:28.730 --> 00:44:29.814
WAITING FOR GODOT

00:44:34.402 --> 00:44:37.572
What a liar.
He said he'd come if I waited.

00:44:44.579 --> 00:44:47.290
WAITING FOR GODOT

00:44:49.834 --> 00:44:51.294
Oh… So hot.

00:44:56.549 --> 00:44:58.927
Why do you never see him
even though you come every year?

00:44:59.010 --> 00:45:01.137
But you watch that damn play every time.

00:45:03.473 --> 00:45:05.600
I just watch it for old times' sake.

00:45:07.894 --> 00:45:09.020
We had so much fun then.

00:45:13.900 --> 00:45:14.734
Ji-woo.

00:45:15.610 --> 00:45:17.362
Are you really not going to see Kyeong-do?

00:45:20.657 --> 00:45:21.991
Se-yeong, you see…

00:45:23.159 --> 00:45:26.621
I thought it was wrong after our breakup
so I went to see him.

00:45:28.206 --> 00:45:31.459
He wanted to buy me a pork cutlet,
so I was going to ask him to buy it.

00:45:31.543 --> 00:45:36.256
While sitting in that restaurant,
I was going to call Kyeong-do.

00:45:36.339 --> 00:45:39.676
And an older couple
were having the pork cutlet next to me.

00:45:39.759 --> 00:45:40.969
It must've been her birthday.

00:45:41.719 --> 00:45:45.139
The man bought her a 50,000-won blouse.

00:45:45.223 --> 00:45:49.143
And the woman nagged at him
for buying something so expensive.

00:45:51.271 --> 00:45:53.273
She seemed to like it though.

00:45:53.356 --> 00:45:55.942
What are you talking about
all of a sudden?

00:45:57.235 --> 00:46:00.822
They were Kyeong-do's parents.

00:46:03.074 --> 00:46:03.992
What?

00:46:05.201 --> 00:46:06.661
They were talking to him on the phone.

00:46:08.204 --> 00:46:11.332
That's when I understood
what Kyeong-do meant.

00:46:13.710 --> 00:46:16.754
There is a life I'm not aware of.

00:46:18.172 --> 00:46:20.425
And I'll never know.

00:46:20.508 --> 00:46:23.678
Every time that happens,
I'll hurt Kyeong-do's feelings.

00:46:24.512 --> 00:46:26.014
Then we'll end up

00:46:27.140 --> 00:46:28.558
hurting each other again.

00:46:36.357 --> 00:46:39.027
WAITING FOR GODOT
THE LAST SHOW

00:46:39.110 --> 00:46:41.487
The curtain's closed.

00:46:42.363 --> 00:46:43.615
I should end it as well.

00:46:46.492 --> 00:46:48.828
With my idiot Kyeong-do.

00:46:51.831 --> 00:46:53.708
Every time I watch it,

00:46:54.459 --> 00:46:56.210
I think it's long and hard to understand.

00:46:58.171 --> 00:47:00.757
I still can't believe you watched it
so many times.

00:47:02.675 --> 00:47:04.761
Hey, then can you tell

00:47:04.844 --> 00:47:07.889
what social absurdity is
just by looking at it?

00:47:14.854 --> 00:47:17.732
But how come
we've never run into each other?

00:47:19.400 --> 00:47:20.777
Maybe one of us is lying.

00:47:21.402 --> 00:47:24.280
Then you're lying.
I even wrote an article about it.

00:47:24.822 --> 00:47:26.324
I'm not lying either.

00:47:37.418 --> 00:47:38.544
What?

00:47:42.799 --> 00:47:45.593
Godot, you, and me,

00:47:45.677 --> 00:47:48.721
we must have missed each other so fiercely
to end up here now.

00:47:58.564 --> 00:47:59.607
I got something for you.

00:48:25.466 --> 00:48:27.385
I wanted to ask you.

00:48:29.303 --> 00:48:32.724
I always wanted to ask you if you had it.

00:48:34.225 --> 00:48:35.268
Why didn't you?

00:48:42.024 --> 00:48:43.776
Because you'd be in pain,

00:48:45.069 --> 00:48:47.071
and so would I.

00:48:53.786 --> 00:48:55.371
Don't leave me now.

00:48:56.664 --> 00:48:57.582
Or I'll die.

00:49:48.800 --> 00:49:50.343
Triple the dosage.

00:50:03.606 --> 00:50:04.607
Drink it while it's warm.

00:50:13.199 --> 00:50:14.784
This medicine is kind of bitter.

00:50:16.244 --> 00:50:18.246
This is your favorite chocolate.

00:50:18.329 --> 00:50:20.289
I went to buy some myself this morning.

00:50:26.879 --> 00:50:28.840
I'll drink it later.

00:50:33.803 --> 00:50:36.722
It's only effective when it's warm.

00:50:40.643 --> 00:50:43.104
Come on, don't be like Ro-a.

00:50:46.107 --> 00:50:49.193
Even if it's bitter,
endure it and drink it up.

00:50:49.277 --> 00:50:50.903
I used good deer antlers.

00:51:29.108 --> 00:51:29.942
LEE GANG-HYEON

00:51:32.987 --> 00:51:34.822
Oh, my. Oh, no.

00:51:34.906 --> 00:51:35.740
Is your hand okay?

00:51:35.823 --> 00:51:38.951
Yes, I'm okay. Honey. Sorry.

00:51:39.452 --> 00:51:40.286
Okay.

00:51:41.829 --> 00:51:42.830
Yes, Executive Lee.

00:51:45.291 --> 00:51:46.125
Yes.

00:51:54.258 --> 00:51:55.217
Yes.

00:52:21.661 --> 00:52:22.745
Hello.

00:52:24.038 --> 00:52:25.581
DONGWOON DAILY
LEE KYEONG-DO

00:52:25.665 --> 00:52:28.459
Can you check if there's a graduate
named Yoo Dan-bi?

00:52:28.542 --> 00:52:32.296
We can't provide personal information
at our discretion.

00:52:32.380 --> 00:52:33.255
Then,

00:52:34.340 --> 00:52:36.634
can you just check
if she graduated from here?

00:52:37.218 --> 00:52:38.094
That is--

00:52:38.177 --> 00:52:41.722
I'm not trying to
write an article about it. Please?

00:52:46.268 --> 00:52:47.395
What year did she enter?

00:52:50.356 --> 00:52:52.858
EDUCATION
ENROLLMENT PERIOD

00:52:53.734 --> 00:52:54.610
Here.

00:52:58.906 --> 00:53:02.201
There is no graduate named Yoo Dan-bi.

00:53:13.087 --> 00:53:15.423
Do I report to you from now on?

00:53:16.173 --> 00:53:17.008
Yes.

00:53:18.634 --> 00:53:20.052
Is the pork cutlet good?

00:53:20.136 --> 00:53:22.096
Yes. Do you want a piece?

00:53:23.514 --> 00:53:24.473
Yes.

00:53:27.143 --> 00:53:28.394
Everything is tasty here.

00:53:28.894 --> 00:53:30.396
Bae Jun-soo went to the US.

00:53:31.731 --> 00:53:33.566
And he stopped meeting Kang Min-woo.

00:53:35.401 --> 00:53:38.195
The M&A expert investor.
Is he in Manhattan?

00:53:38.279 --> 00:53:39.572
I think so.

00:53:40.239 --> 00:53:41.115
Should I go?

00:53:41.198 --> 00:53:42.742
Why bother going that far?

00:53:51.417 --> 00:53:54.795
Follow this person, from where she lives
to what she does after work.

00:53:54.879 --> 00:53:55.963
YOO DAN-BI

00:53:57.465 --> 00:53:59.842
Watch all her followers
and every story she posts.

00:54:00.593 --> 00:54:01.427
Okay.

00:54:02.928 --> 00:54:03.846
Is the gimbap good?

00:54:05.347 --> 00:54:06.307
Yes.

00:54:15.066 --> 00:54:16.192
Teacher,

00:54:17.902 --> 00:54:18.986
I'm okay

00:54:19.945 --> 00:54:22.448
with the integral calculus questions,

00:54:23.365 --> 00:54:25.242
but I'm stuck with geometry.

00:54:27.703 --> 00:54:28.537
Really?

00:54:41.008 --> 00:54:44.470
I marked them. I got everything right.

00:54:46.514 --> 00:54:49.308
You're at an academy, aren't you?

00:54:51.227 --> 00:54:54.438
I have English after math.

00:54:55.815 --> 00:54:58.442
Then you need to move
to the other class, right?

00:54:58.526 --> 00:54:59.401
Yes.

00:55:01.821 --> 00:55:02.947
My workbooks.

00:55:04.198 --> 00:55:05.199
Okay.

00:55:09.120 --> 00:55:10.121
Here.

00:55:13.415 --> 00:55:15.209
-Do you want to go to the class?
-Okay.

00:55:17.586 --> 00:55:18.838
Oh, wait.

00:55:23.676 --> 00:55:24.593
Secretary Cha,

00:55:24.677 --> 00:55:27.471
can you grab the report from my room?

00:55:28.139 --> 00:55:30.891
Don't send Secretary Yoo.
It's confidential.

00:55:31.767 --> 00:55:32.726
Bye.

00:55:36.981 --> 00:55:38.065
All right.

00:55:38.649 --> 00:55:39.733
-Let's go.
-Okay.

00:55:50.661 --> 00:55:51.704
Come on.

00:55:54.707 --> 00:55:56.667
My English teacher…

00:55:57.835 --> 00:55:59.128
Why would they...

00:56:05.634 --> 00:56:07.511
I'm here to meet CEO Seo Ji-yeon.

00:56:07.595 --> 00:56:08.804
One second.

00:56:11.432 --> 00:56:15.352
Mr. Lee Kyeong-do is here to meet the CEO.
Yes, okay.

00:56:18.439 --> 00:56:20.065
-At two o'clock, right?
-Yes.

00:56:20.149 --> 00:56:24.153
The CEO isn't available at the moment.
Can you wait a moment?

00:56:24.236 --> 00:56:25.362
Oh, okay. Sure.

00:56:37.124 --> 00:56:38.667
This isn't the classroom.

00:56:38.751 --> 00:56:42.796
It's right around the corner.
Go on. Let's go. Come.

00:56:55.309 --> 00:56:56.435
Isn't that Ms. Seo?

00:57:19.458 --> 00:57:20.376
Let me help you.

00:57:23.545 --> 00:57:24.755
Don't you steal mine…

00:57:32.096 --> 00:57:33.097
Ji-yeon. What's wrong?

00:58:27.276 --> 00:58:30.237
Please be seated.

00:58:30.904 --> 00:58:34.575
Waiting for Godot will start soon.

00:58:41.457 --> 00:58:42.416
Sorry.

00:59:08.275 --> 00:59:09.526
WAITING FOR GODOT

00:59:34.760 --> 00:59:35.803
Hurry up.

00:59:36.303 --> 00:59:39.348
JANGCHUNG SNACK BAR

01:01:54.775 --> 01:01:57.110
When I went to meet you at the airport,
I was thinking,

01:01:57.903 --> 01:01:59.738
Only if you don't leave.

01:01:59.821 --> 01:02:03.283
Was I the only immature kid?

01:02:03.367 --> 01:02:05.786
Seo Ji-yeon's dementia,
Seo Ji-woo being an illegitimate child...

01:02:06.662 --> 01:02:09.831
Where that asshole is going,
I have to be there first.

01:02:10.791 --> 01:02:14.586
If Ji-woo really puts her mind to it,
even ten guys couldn't take her down.

01:02:15.170 --> 01:02:18.715
An illegitimate child out of wedlock.
It's a nice keyword.

01:02:20.133 --> 01:02:21.093
Let's get ahead of him.

01:02:21.176 --> 01:02:22.928
You did earn the assistant manager title.

01:02:24.054 --> 01:02:24.972
Just show yourself.

01:02:25.639 --> 01:02:27.849
Just as I am.